            "b": 0.28627450980392155,
            "a": 0.8
          },
          "text": "Geographic projections transform the Earth's 3D surface onto a 2D plane. This process inevitably introduces distortions. Projections affect the shapes, area, distance, or direction of boundaries and locations.  ",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontColor": {
            "r": 0.9333333333333333,
            "g": 0.9333333333333333,
            "b": 0.9333333333333333,
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "egih3UyNsS5:15",
          "type": "STICKY",
          "x": 790,
          "y": 510,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 130,
          "backgroundColor": {
            "r": 0.03137254901960784,
            "g": 0.1843137254901961,
            "b": 0.28627450980392155,
            "a": 0.8
          },
          "text": "The AlbersUSA projection is a special case of the Albers Equal-Area Conic projection, designed to represent the entire United States, including the contiguous 48 states, Alaska, and Hawaii. It minimizes distortions by applying separate conic projections for different regions. This method preserves the relative sizes (areas) of each state and adjusts the positions of Alaska and Hawaii to make it easier to display the U.S. on a single map.",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontColor": {
            "r": 0.9333333333333333,
            "g": 0.9333333333333333,
            "b": 0.9333333333333333,
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "egih3UyNsS5:16",
          "type": "STICKY",
          "x": 790,
          "y": 440,
          "width": 300,
          "height": 60,
          "backgroundColor": {
            "r": 0.03137254901960784,
            "g": 0.1843137254901961,
            "b": 0.28627450980392155,
            "a": 0.8
          },
          "text": "Switch the projection to Albers and set the scale to 100, Rotate lambda to 90 and Translate Y to 100. Notice the position and the dimensions of Hawaii and Alaska. ",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontColor": {
            "r": 0.9333333333333333,
            "g": 0.9333333333333333,
            "b": 0.9333333333333333,
            "a": 1
          }
        },
